  "nameStory": "",
  "description": "The Cuban Ground Cricket is a small, dark-colored cricket belonging to the family Trigonidiidae, commonly found in leaf litter and ground vegetation throughout New England. Despite its tropical name, this species has established populations in northeastern North America where it thrives in moist, sheltered microhabitats.",
